  "question": {
    "text": "The activation energy for a reaction which doubles the rate when the temperature is raised from $298 \\mathrm{~K}$ to $308 \\mathrm{~K}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "f1PzO",
      "text": "\n$59.2 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dxjgA",
      "text": "\n$39.2 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "s8Qz1",
      "text": "\n$52.9 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Z8BNF",
      "text": "\n$29.5 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Activation energy can be calculated from the equation.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{\\log K_2}{\\log K_1}=\\frac{-E_a}{2.303 R}\\left(\\frac{1}{T_2}-\\frac{1}{T_1}\\right) \\\\\n& \\text { Given } \\frac{\\log K_2}{\\log K_1}=2 \\quad T_2=308 ; \\quad T_1=298 \\\\\n& \\therefore \\quad \\log 2=\\frac{-E_a}{2.303 \\times 8.314}\\left(\\frac{1}{308}-\\frac{1}{298}\\right) \\\\\n& E_a=52.9 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
